dma-proxy-sha3 — kernel driver for the SHA-3 accelerator
========================================================

Kernel module that feeds the SHA-3 AXI-Stream IP core through AXI DMA in
scatter-gather mode. It exposes two userspace interfaces:

  * zero-copy   — userspace pins its own buffers, the driver maps them for
                  DMA directly (tool: ../../C/user-space_files/sha3_hash_zerocopy.c)
  * legacy mmap — buffers allocated by the driver on the ALLOC_BUFFERS ioctl
                  and mmap'd into userspace (tool: sha3_hash_legacy.c)

Build (PetaLinux)
-----------------
The module is packaged by the Yocto recipe ../../dma-proxy-sha3.bb:

    petalinux-build -c dma-proxy-sha3

or, against an already built kernel tree:

    make -C <kernel-src> M=$(pwd)

Device tree
-----------
The driver binds to:

    dma_proxy_sha3 {
        compatible = "xlnx,dma_proxy_sha3";
        dmas = <&axi_dma_0 0 &axi_dma_0 1>;
        dma-names = "tx_channel", "rx_channel";
    };

Load
----
    insmod dma-proxy-sha3.ko

